  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Performance Rail",
    "overview": "The waveform display acts like an instrument: quiet near-black structure makes frequency bands, timing and cue positions immediately legible. The user selected the XDJ-AZ as the visual reference. This documents the implemented Python/Tk/SDL system, not a claim of pixel-identical hardware reproduction.\n\nDensity comes from aligned signal and marker rails, with native controls in a separate settings window. The provisional draft is refreshed from `rb_waveform_core/config.py`, `render.py`, `rb_waveform_gpu.py`, `cues.py`, and `rkbx_wave.py`; the source now takes precedence over its earlier proposed palette. Native fonts and widget chrome may vary by platform.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Signal first, with restrained structural chrome.",
      "Consistent timing geometry across equal-height deck lanes.",
      "Frequency and cue colors carry meaning.",
      "Playback drives motion; controls remain native and separate."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Semantic Color Rule",
        "body": "Frequency, cue and timing colors identify data; do not reuse them as decorative accents.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Saved Is Not Active Rule",
        "body": "A saved-loop bracket indicates stored endpoints only. No active-loop engagement state is supplied to this renderer; do not imply that the loop is currently running.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the shared track-time transform for waveform, beat, cue and loop positions.",
      "**Do** retain physical deck identity when rows are reordered or the deck count changes.",
      "**Do** keep native focus and labels usable in the separate settings window.",
      "**Do** distinguish synthetic demo, offline analysis and live input states."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use semantic signal and cue colors as decorative accents.",
      "**Don't** imply a saved loop is engaged without a verified active-loop state.",
      "**Don't** claim direct macOS live synchronization from a successful demo render.",
      "**Don't** introduce decorative motion or elevation into the waveform canvas."
    ]
  }
}
